":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions — Israel","noes":33,"question":"Ron Boswell I move: That the Senate— (a) condemns the boycott of Israel instigated by Marrickville Council—part of the Global Boycott Divestments and Sanctions—banning any links with Israeli organisations or organisations that support Israel and prohibiting any academic, government, sporting or cultural exchanges with Israel; (b) acknowledges that Israel is a legitimate and democratic state and a good friend of Australia; and (c) denounces the Israeli boycott by Marrickville Council and others, and condemns any expansion of it. Bob Brown I seek leave to move an amendment to that motion. Leave granted. I thank the Senate and I move the following amendment: Omit all words after \"That\", substitute, \"the Senate recognises the rights of the people of Palestine and Israel to live together as self-governing states based on the 1967 borders. For clarity, the motion would then read in its entirety: That the Senate recognises the rights of the people of Palestine and Israel to live together as self-governing states based on the 1967 borders. Barnaby Joyce Mr Deputy President, I rise on a point of order. Can you give us a ruling on whether that completely changes the nature of the motion and therefore should be ruled out? Stephen Parry It is relevant to the motion, Senator Joyce, but it does change the entire context of the motion. That is what the Senate will now vote on. Question put: That the amendment (Senator Brown's) be agreed to. The Senate divided. [16:31] (The Deputy PRESIDENT—Senator Parry) Question negatived.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-2021","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2011-07-05/2"}
